{% extends "base.twig" %}

{# The front page renders its blocks straight into .site-content, with no wrapper.

   IX's base.twig already opens <main class="site-main"> and emits post.content
   inside .site-content, so a wrapper here would nest a second <main> — two
   landmarks, invalid HTML — and, less obviously, break the full-bleed breakout.

   IX matches `.site-content > .alignfull` with a child combinator (see
   common/_layout.scss). A wrapper makes every section a grandchild, the
   selector stops matching, and full-width sections silently cap at content
   width. On a page built from alignfull section groups that is the whole
   layout, and it fails quietly — the markup looks right and nothing errors.

   Overriding the block rather than deleting it: the effect is identical to
   letting base.twig's default run, but saying it explicitly keeps this comment
   where the next person will look. #}
{% block content %}
    {{ post.content }}
{% endblock %}
